MzTabExporter -- Exports various OpenMS XML and parquet formats to an mzTab file.
Full documentation: http://www.openms.de/doxygen/release/4.0.0/html/TOPP_MzTabExporter.html
Version: 1.0.0 (OpenMS core 4.0.0, revision 4fdec46)
To cite OpenMS:
 + Pfeuffer, J., Bielow, C., Wein, S. et al.. OpenMS 3 enables reproducible analysis of large-scale mass spectrometry data. Nat Methods (2024). doi:10.1038/s41592-024-02197-7.

Usage:
  MzTabExporter <options>

Options (mandatory options marked with '*'):
  -in <file>           Input files used to generate the mzTab file. (valid formats: 'featureXML', 'featureparquet', 'consensusXML', 'consensusparquet', 'idXML', 'idparquet', 'mzid')
  -out <file>*         Output file (mzTab) (valid formats: 'mzTab')
  -opt_columns <mods>  Add optional columns which are not part of the mzTab standard. (default: '[subfeatures]') (valid: 'subfeatures')
                       
Common TOPP options:
  -ini <file>          Use the given TOPP INI file
  -threads <n>         Sets the number of threads allowed to be used by the TOPP tool (0 = all available cores) (default: '1')
  -write_ini <file>    Writes the default configuration file
  --help               Shows options
  --helphelp           Shows all options (including advanced)

